}
```

In this example, we define an array called `array` with some elements. Then, we use a `for...of` loop to iterate over each element in the array. The loop variable `element` takes on the value of each array element in turn, and we can perform any desired operation on it.

Feel free to replace the `console.log(element)` statement with your own code to process each array element as needed.

This approach is commonly used to iterate over arrays in JavaScript, and it provides a concise and readable way to loop through all the elements in an array.

