}
}</p>

<p>The main difference between a class and a struct is that a class is a reference type and a struct is a value type. This means that when you create an instance of a class, you are actually creating a reference to the object, whereas when you create an instance of a struct, you are creating a copy of the struct.</p>

<p>Another difference is that a class can have constructors, whereas a struct cannot. A struct can only have a single constructor, which is called the default constructor. A class can have multiple constructors.</p>

<p>Finally, a class can inherit from another class, whereas a struct cannot.</p>

