```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Minimum Length Validation</title>
    <script>
        function validateForm() {
            var inputField = document.getElementById('inputField');
            var minLength = 5; // Set your desired minimum length here

            if (inputField.value.length < minLength) {
                alert('Please enter at least ' + minLength + ' characters.');
                return false;
            }

            return true;
        }
    </script>
</head>
<body>
    <form onsubmit="return validateForm()">
        <label for="inputField">Enter text:</label>
        <input type="text" id="inputField" name="inputField">
        <input type="submit" value="Submit">
    </form>
</body>
</html>
```

In this example, the `validateForm` function checks if the length of the input field's value is less than the specified minimum length (in this case, 5 characters). If it is, an alert is displayed, and the form submission is prevented.

If you prefer server-side validation, you can use Python or another server-side language to validate the input on the server side. Here's an example using Flask, a popular Python web framework:

```python
from flask import Flask, request, render_template

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/', methods=['GET', 'POST'])
def form():
    if request.method == 'POST':
        input_value = request.form['inputField']
        min_length = 5  # Set your desired minimum length here

        if len(input_value) < min_length:
            return render_template('error.html', message='Please enter at least ' + str(min_length) + ' characters.')

        # Proceed with further processing...
        return 'Form submitted successfully.'

    return render_template('form.html')

if __name__ == '__main__':
    app.run(debug=True)
```

In this example, the `form` function checks the length of the input value on the server side and returns an error message if it is less than the specified minimum length. You can customize the error message and further processing based on your needs.

