Title: Check if inputs are empty using jQuery.
Body: <p>I have a form that I would like all fields to be filled in. If a field is clicked into and then not filled out, I would like to display a red background. </p>

<p>Here is my code:</p>

<pre><code>$('#apply-form input').blur(function () {
  if ($('input:text').is(":empty")) {
    $(this).parents('p').addClass('warning');
  }
});
</code></pre>

<p>It applies the warning class regardless of the field being filled in or not.</p>

<p>What am I doing wrong?</p>

Answers:
It looks like you're trying to check if the input field is empty or not. However, your code is checking if all input fields are empty, which is not what you want.

Instead, you can check if the current input field is empty or not. Here's the updated code:

```javascript
$('#apply-form input').blur(function () {
  if ($(this).is(":empty")) {
    $(this).parents('p').addClass('warning');
  }
});
```

This code checks if the current input field is empty and adds the warning class if it is.

You can also use the `:visible` selector to check if the input field is visible or not. Here's an updated code:

```javascript
$('#apply-form input').blur(function () {
  if ($(this).is(":empty") && $(this).is(":visible")) {
    $(this).parents('p').addClass('warning');
  }
});
```

This code checks if the current input field is empty and visible before adding the warning class.

You can also use the `:focus` selector to check if the input field is focused or not. Here's an updated code:

```javascript
$('#apply-form input').focusout(function () {
  if ($(this).is(":empty") && $(this).is(":focus")) {
    $(this).parents('p').addClass('warning');
  }
});
```

This code checks if the current input field is empty and focused before adding the warning class.

You can also use the `:invalid` selector to check if the input field is invalid or not. Here's an updated code:

```javascript
$('#apply-form input').blur(function () {
  if ($(this).is(":invalid")) {
    $(this).parents('p').addClass('warning');
  }
});
```

This code checks if the current input field is invalid before adding the warning class. 

